# Trivy CVE allowlist for the wolf-scanners images.
#
# Each entry is a CVE/GHSA ID, one per line. Every exception must identify an
# owner, a fixed expiry no more than 180 days away, a reason, and its image
# scope. The release workflow validates this metadata before building.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN # owner=<team/email>; expires=YYYY-MM-DD; reason=<why accepted>; images=<exact-image-scope-or-all>
#
# The release workflow validates this source and renders a separate plain
# Trivy ignore file for each scanner, fixer, runtime, proposal, and adapter
# image. An exception scoped to one image can therefore never suppress the
# same vulnerability ID in another image.
#
# Empty for now — add entries only when a real CVE blocks publishing
# AND the fix isn't available upstream. ignore-unfixed is set in the
# workflow so CVEs without a fix don't fail the build either way.
